# WAAMTO Website Rules v3.0

> Website-specific development rules for all WAAMTO web properties.

---

# Purpose

Build fast, secure, SEO-friendly and consistent websites while protecting the approved WAAMTO brand and architecture.

---

# Scope

Applies to:

- Marketing Website
- Product Website
- Customer Portal (Frontend)
- Documentation Website
- Landing Pages

Modify only the areas relevant to the requested task.

---

# Design

Always:

- Follow the approved design system.
- Reuse existing components.
- Maintain responsive layouts.
- Keep UI clean and consistent.

Do not redesign pages unless requested.

---

# Branding

Preserve:

- Logo
- Colours
- Typography
- Icons
- Brand language

Never introduce inconsistent branding.

---

# Content

Keep content:

- Accurate
- Professional
- Consistent
- SEO-friendly

Do not change business messaging unless requested.

---

# Performance

Optimise where appropriate:

- Images
- Fonts
- Bundle size
- Lazy loading
- Rendering
- Core Web Vitals

Avoid unnecessary JavaScript.

---

# SEO

Preserve or improve:

- Page titles
- Meta descriptions
- Heading hierarchy
- Structured data
- Canonical URLs
- Sitemap
- Internal links

Do not reduce search visibility.

---

# Accessibility

Verify when affected:

- Semantic HTML
- Keyboard navigation
- Colour contrast
- Alt text
- Form labels

---

# Forms

Ensure forms include:

- Validation
- Error handling
- Spam protection
- Secure submission

Never trust client-side validation alone.

---

# Integrations

Maintain compatibility with:

- License Engine
- ERP
- Monitoring
- Analytics
- Contact forms
- Payment services

Verify affected integrations after changes.

---

# Security

Protect:

- User input
- Authentication flows
- Uploaded files
- Sensitive information

Reuse existing security mechanisms.

---

# Testing

Validate reasonably affected areas:

- UI
- Responsive behaviour
- Navigation
- Forms
- SEO-critical elements
- Performance
- Accessibility
- Integration points

Test likely regression paths.

---

# Reporting

Include:

- Scope
- Pages changed
- Validation completed
- Issues found
- Production readiness

Keep reports concise.

